{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1710, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThere are N people, labeled 1 to N. Person i has an integer A_i.\nAmong the people who satisfy the condition \"None of the other N-1 people has the same integer as themselves,\" find the one with the greatest integer, and print that person's label.\nIf no person satisfies the condition, report that fact instead.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nA_1 A_2 \\ldots A_N\n\nOutput\n\nIf no person satisfies the condition \"None of the other N-1 people has the same integer as themselves,\" print -1.\nOtherwise, among those who satisfy it, print the label of the person whose integer is the largest.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 3\\times 10^5\n- 1 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n9\r\n2 9 9 7 9 2 4 5 8\n\nSample Output 1\n\n9\r\n\nThose who satisfy the condition are the persons labeled 4, 7, 8, and 9.\r\nTheir integers are 7, 4, 5, and 8, respectively, and the person with the largest integer is the person labeled 9.\r\nThus, the answer is 9.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\r\n1000000000 1000000000 998244353 998244353\n\nSample Output 2\n\n-1\r\n\nIf no person satisfies the condition, print -1.\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1758, "char_start": 1722, "quote": "Input:\n9\n2 9 9 7 9 2 4 5 8\nOutput:\n9", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1831, "char_start": 1770, "quote": "Input:\n4\n1000000000 1000000000 998244353 998244353\nOutput:\n-1", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "e0538a8f36c3a7a1c789dc192959082f8f18088e0b4bcc19766edbccf50b75a2", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "805bf498e32ccd60bfec9de52b4ad06e871a5ca1889eb01d54567b541973e238", "seq": 2}
